TITLE:: SDGSynthPresets
summary:: a synth's presets as changed in the window, kept on this machine outside the repo
categories:: Libraries>SuperDirtGUI
related:: Classes/SuperDirtGUI, Classes/SDGWindow

DESCRIPTION::
A synth's presets are its events in SuperDirt's sound library, the ones Tidal's code::n:: picks
(code::s "sdgkick:3"::). Its file registers them. When you press save as... or delete in the
window's synth preview, the synth's whole new list is written to a file of its own in
link::#*folder::, the user support directory, and from then on that list replaces the one the
synth's file registers - when the file is read again, and in every later session.

The list stays outside the repo on purpose: updating the quark never clashes with it, and a
student's presets survive a reinstall. file presets in the window, or
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-restoreFilePresets::, deletes the file and brings back the synth's own list.

The file is plain SuperCollider, one preset a line, and can be edited by hand. A preset holds
its code::presetName:: and the synth's controls, nothing else; SuperDirtGUI puts each one on top
of what the file's first preset holds besides those (code::instrument::, code::note: 0::, a drum
voice's code::unitDuration::), so a saved drum preset still rings as long as the voice does.

code::
SDGSynthPresets.folder.openOS;      // where they are
SDGSynthPresets.read(\sdgkick);     // nil until a preset of sdgkick was saved or deleted
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: folder
Where the files are: code::Platform.userAppSupportDir +/+ "superdirt-gui-presets":: unless set.
Checks set it to a scratch folder.
ARGUMENT:: path
a folder; made when the first file is written.

METHOD:: fileFor
The file of a synth's list, code::<folder>/<synth>.scd::, whether it exists or not.
ARGUMENT:: synth
the synth's name.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/String::

METHOD:: exists
Whether the synth plays this machine's list.
ARGUMENT:: synth
the synth's name.
RETURNS:: a link::Classes/Boolean::

METHOD:: read
The synth's list, each preset an link::Classes/Event:: of code::presetName:: and controls.
ARGUMENT:: synth
the synth's name.
RETURNS:: an link::Classes/Array::, or nil when there is no file or it could not be read (that
is posted, and the synth's own presets play).

METHOD:: write
Write a synth's list, replacing the file. SuperDirtGUI calls it; use
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-savePreset:: and link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-removePreset::, which
also put the list into the sound library.
ARGUMENT:: synth
the synth's name.
ARGUMENT:: list
Events of code::presetName:: and controls.
RETURNS:: the file's path.

METHOD:: forget
Delete the synth's file. The sound library keeps what it holds until
link::Classes/SuperDirtGUI#-restoreFilePresets:: or the synth's file is read again.
ARGUMENT:: synth
the synth's name.
